# Build context for the production image (see Dockerfile).
#
# Two rules of thumb behind the exclusions:
#   1. Never ship secrets or live state — `.env`, databases, logs, the data root.
#   2. Never ship anything the build regenerates — node_modules, dist, venvs.
# Everything the image needs is `backend/`, `frontend/` sources and the two
# dependency manifests under `ops/docker/`.

# --- Secrets & live state (must never enter an image layer) ----------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example
*.pem
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal

# --- Runtime / deployment state --------------------------------------------
logs/
run/
var/
media/
staticfiles/
backend/media/
backend/staticfiles/

# --- The data root. Volumes are bind-mounted at runtime, never baked in. ----
data/
mito_data_root/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.npy
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.h5
*.hdf5

# --- Model weights. ~1 GB of Git LFS; mounted read-only at runtime instead
#     (see docker-compose.yml), so `git lfs pull` is not a build prerequisite.
vendor/

# --- Regenerated by the build ----------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
dist/
build/
venv/
.venv/

# --- Python noise -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.log
*.pid

# --- VCS, docs, editor, local tooling --------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.claude/
.dev-cache/
*.swp
*~
*.backup.[0-9]*
docs/
progress/
frontend/e2e/
frontend/phase14-harness.html
frontend/playwright*.config.ts
docker-compose*.yml
